### Bundled third-party binaries (M2)

The KataGo engine and neural-net weights are downloaded at build time into
`apps/desktop/resources/` and shipped inside the installer (ADR 0003, D6). They
are not npm packages, so the license gate (`check:licenses`) does not see them;
this ledger is the D4 provenance record for that payload.

**KataGo engine** — [lightvector/KataGo](https://github.com/lightvector/KataGo),
release [v1.18.1](https://github.com/lightvector/KataGo/releases/tag/v1.18.1),
**MIT license** ("Copyright 2025 David J Wu … and/or other authors"). KataGo
vendors third-party components under their own licenses inside `cpp/external`
(clblast, cutlass, nlohmann_json, httplib, onnx, tclap, and others — see the
upstream LICENSE preamble); those ride along inside the binary unchanged.

**KataGo neural-net weights** — [katagotraining.org](https://katagotraining.org/)
distributed-training nets, **CC0-1.0** for the g170 imported nets (the bundled
b6c96 and the b10c128 alternative are g170 finals; the kata1-run nets carry a
separate MIT-style license but are not what M2 bundles). CC0 waives attribution;
provenance is recorded here regardless. The exact net
(`kata1-b6c96-s175395328-d26788732.txt.gz`) is pinned in
`scripts/katago-manifest.ts`.

Neither payload publishes an upstream checksum, so the fetch scripts record a
GoMentor-side sha256 at first download (trust-on-first-use) and verify against
it thereafter; see `scripts/katago-manifest.ts`.

